 "_corrected_2026_10_08": "THE SAME BUG ONE LEVEL DEEPER, AND THE 2026-10-06 FIX IS WHY IT SURVIVED. That fix made the key a real SHA and left the REFERENT wrong: the gate recorded flags computed over the WHOLE PUSH RANGE under the push TIP. So a row asserted that the tip commit changed files it does not contain, while the commit that really changed them got no row. DISCARDED, NOT APPLIED: 20 rows parked across five stashes in Documents/SAIRN-hank (\"cc scrutiny rows\", rounds 2-6). They are 3 distinct paths re-keyed against 7 shas -- the same push refused and rewritten six times. 6 of the 7 shas are ORPHANED in hank's OWN clone (verified there, not inferred from absence here). The 7th, bf174f30, resolves and is an ancestor of origin/main, and its 3 rows are still WRONG: it changes five docs files and NONE of the three paths they name. Subject-matching the orphans to their landed replacements is provably ambiguous -- two orphans share the subject \"the three records this batch's fixes owe\" and no landed commit carries it -- so no re-seat was attempted and none was guessed. BACKFILLED FROM THE REAL COMMITS INSTEAD, which is stronger than copying a stashed row: the classifier was run against each landed commit's OWN diff. The 20 rows reduce to FOUR facts -- 320ddabe tests/run_tool_usage_refusal_probe.py WEAKENING, 72d757ef tests/run_audit_event_type_probe.py WEAKENING, 4ec0d5d5 and 56bbce5e tests/sd_data_write_attribution_three_apps.js CHANGE. Every one is self-verifiable: git show <sha> -- <path> produces a diff. NOT RETROACTIVELY COMPLETE, SAID PLAINLY: only the commits those stashes were about were backfilled. Earlier origin/main commits that touched a self-checking file while the tip-keyed bug was live are still unflagged, and this file does not know which. FIXED IN THE GENERATOR: tools/sairn_push_gate_hook.py now keys per COMMIT from that commit's own diff, and prints COULD NOT ATTRIBUTE rather than keying to the tip when no single commit produces the flags. Locked by tests/run_scrutiny_flag_probe.py arm G -- a two-commit push with the weakening in the first and a docs-only tip -- which every arm before it could not express, because they all pushed exactly one commit so `tip` and `the commit that changed it` were the same object. Ablated against the pre-fix gate via SCRUT_PROBE_GATE: 4 of arm G's 9 checks go red and the row sha comes back equal to the tip.",
 "_corrected_2026_10_08b": "FORTY-EIGHT ROWS REMOVED AS PROVABLY FALSE, and a validator added so this cannot accumulate again. The 2026-10-08 correction above fixed the GENERATOR -- flags are now keyed per commit from that commit's own diff -- and said plainly that it was NOT retroactive. This is the retroactive half, done with a check rather than by hand. MEASURED by tools/scrutiny_ledger_check.py over all 114 rows: HOLDS 24, CONTRADICTED 30, MERGE_KEYED 18, UNRESOLVABLE 42, MALFORMED 0, duplicate identities 0. The 48 findings were removed; the 24 that hold and the 42 that cannot be checked in this clone were kept. CONTRADICTED means the sha resolves, is a single-parent commit, and its diff for that path is EMPTY -- the row accuses a commit of a change it does not contain. MERGE_KEYED IS REPORTED SEPARATELY AND THAT MATTERS: `git show` prints no diff for a merge commit, so an empty result there proves nothing either way, and calling it a contradiction would be a true sentence pointing at the wrong cause -- the same misdiagnosis fixed in the D9 gate message this same day. A merge authors no change, so it is never the commit in which a checker was edited; the row is wrong for that reason instead. The dropped rows were overwhelmingly keyed to merge commits, handoff commits and bookkeeping commits -- i.e. to push TIPS -- which is the signature of the defect the generator fix removed. NOTHING TRUE WAS LOST: a row whose named commit does not contain the named change is false, and deleting a false row discards no information. What IS still missing is the flags those pushes really owed, and they are not recoverable from here -- the same disclosure the 2026-10-08 note already carries. UNRESOLVABLE IS NOT A FINDING AND IS KEPT: a row can legitimately name a commit this clone has never fetched, and a validator that failed on one would be out of the merge policy within a week. VALIDATOR NOW DECLARED in merge_policy, which closes the gap that made tools/sairn_rebase_resolve.py exit 2 on this file's conflicts and forced a hand merge on 2026-10-08.",
 "_corrected_2026_10_06": "NINE ROWS KEYED \"main\" WERE REMOVED. The push gate handed its prepush `tip`, which is a REF NAME, not a sha -- so the (sha, path) identity could never dedup them and no rewrite map could ever re-seat them. Found by reading this file, not by reading the code that wrote it. Guarded in two places since: the gate resolves tip to a sha, and scrutiny_record refuses a non-sha key outright."
}
